{"id":"n-california","name":"Northern California","country":"United States","story":"Wildland–urban interface fires: Camp (2018), August Complex and North Complex (2020), Dixie (2021).","places":["California","Butte County","Paradise"],"lang":["en","es"],"bbox":[-123.5,38.5,-120.0,41.5],"grid_deg":0.1,"data_through":"2026-11-10","built_at":"2026-11-10T16:40:37+00:00","estimand":{"primary":"Hotspots per period on the Aqua MODIS scale: the number of vegetation-fire detections Aqua MODIS would have recorded (early-afternoon and post-midnight passes). Day and night are calibrated separately and added.","why_aqua":"The early-afternoon orbit is the only one observed continuously from 2002 (Aqua) through Suomi-NPP, NOAA-20 and NOAA-21. Converting VIIRS to MODIS scale discards information and is well-posed; the reverse must invent small fires MODIS never saw, so the VIIRS-scale view is marked modelled before 2012.","secondary":["Fire cell-days (0.1° cell × UTC day with ≥1 detection), Aqua scale","Hotspots on the Suomi-NPP VIIRS scale (modelled before 2012)","Persistent heat sources (kilns, flares, industry, volcanoes) harmonized separately","Raw detections — not comparable across satellite eras"],"not":"Not burned area and not a count of fires: a detection is one hot pixel in one overpass."},"method":{"confidence_filter":"drop VIIRS 'l' and MODIS confidence < 30 (no crosswalk between the two scales); sensitivity reported","static_mask":"0.01° cells where science-quality FIRMS `type` is 1–3 for ≥50% of ≥3 detections","coverage":"share of days each satellite delivered data anywhere on Earth in each period (measured, so launches, gaps and the Suomi-NPP end come from the data); below 25% a satellite is left out, otherwise counts are divided by coverage","calibration":"ratio of totals per calendar month, day and night separately, shrunk toward the pooled ratio by empirical Bayes (shrinkage strength estimated from the data). Chain: Terra→Aqua (2002–2020, bridges 2000–2002 only), 